INT. FIDELITY PRUDENTIAL MUTUAL, CLAIMS DEPARTMENT - DAY

A sea of identical desks and green-shaded lamps. Typewriters clatter in unison. Above the manager's glass-walled office hangs a banner: A SMILE IS A CLAIM WELL-FILED.

MISS GWENDOLYN TILLMAN (30s, cat-eye glasses, ledger in hand) stands before the manager's desk. Behind it sits MR. HORATIO PEMBERTON-HALE (50s, pinstripe, pencil moustache), who hasn't looked up from his blotter.

A MAN IN A GRAY SUIT (40s, bowler, no briefcase) stands at the window with his back to them.

PEMBERTON-HALE
Miss Tillman, your productivity is down four percent.

GWENDOLYN
Mr. Pemberton-Hale, I processed eleven hundred claims.

PEMBERTON-HALE
Eleven hundred and four were expected.

GWENDOLYN
There were four holidays.

PEMBERTON-HALE
Then the holidays are down four percent.

He still hasn't looked up. The Man in the Gray Suit turns from the window, smiling at no one.

GRAY MAN
Don't mind me.

PEMBERTON-HALE
(not looking)
We don't.

The desk phone rings. Pemberton-Hale lifts it without taking his eyes from the blotter.

PEMBERTON-HALE (CONT'D)
(into phone)
Claims.

VOICE (V.O.)
(over phone, thin and tinny)
Horatio. It's Head Office. Is the efficiency man there yet?

PEMBERTON-HALE
(into phone)
Who?

VOICE (V.O.)
The efficiency man. Mr. Alistair Voss. Gray suit, bowler. He's to review the department.

Pemberton-Hale's pencil stops. He looks up, slowly, past Gwendolyn, to the man at the window.

PEMBERTON-HALE
(into phone)
I'll call you back.

He hangs up. Rises. The Man in the Gray Suit takes off his bowler.

PEMBERTON-HALE (CONT'D)
Mr. Voss.

VOSS
Please. Sit. I've been enjoying the show.

Pemberton-Hale does not sit. Neither does Gwendolyn, who has quietly put down her ledger and folded her hands behind her back.

VOSS (CONT'D)
Tell me, Mr. Pemberton-Hale, how many of your employees are four percent down?

PEMBERTON-HALE
One. Miss Tillman.

VOSS
And how many are four percent up?

PEMBERTON-HALE
(a long pause)
None.

VOSS
Then the department is meeting target.

Pemberton-Hale's mouth opens, closes. Gwendolyn picks up her ledger and walks to the door.

GWENDOLYN
Excuse me. I have eleven hundred claims to file.

She closes the glass door behind her very gently. Through the glass, the typewriters clatter on.
